From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] first boot: ask for consent to the anonymous device report

A new first-boot step, after the network one, asks whether RetroForge may send its anonymous
once-per-boot device report (rootfs retroforge-telemetry, docs/telemetry.md). It says what is
sent, and has one toggle, on to start with. Next writes the answer, TELEMETRY=on or off, to
~/.config/retroforge/telemetry.conf, which the report reads: with no file, or off, it never runs.

The step is never skipped: language select goes to it when there is no networking or the device is
online already (where it used to go to the end, or to the plugin step 0039 skips), and the network
step's Next always goes to it. Its Next goes on to the end. B goes back, as on every step.
---
